WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:07.259
Rhodium is a metal which is used very widely
in catalysts. It is

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:13.130
particularly important in chemical reactions
such as the one

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:17.710
that makes ethanoic acid, that is one of the
components of

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.810
vinegar, but it is made industrially from
carbon monoxide and

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:27.099
methanol. And the key components to make this
reaction

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:31.769
work are rhodium compounds, but like many
of the elements

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:38.190
in this part of the periodic table, rhodium
is a very rare metal.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.840
It’s not very widely found in nature and
therefore it is really

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.910
quite expensive and I have been to a catalyst
manufacturer

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.300
and been shown a large vat which they said
has a half a

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.050
million pounds of rhodium compound in, and
when you

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.890
actually look in there is a remarkably small
pile of material at

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:58.330
the bottom.

